---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site } from '../../content/site'
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/ryan-amarit.webp'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Ryan Amarit is an Artist turned Design Engineer and web tech lead in Fort Worth, Texas."
  palette="about"
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero" data-section="about" data-gl="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title" data-split>Artist turned Design Engineer.</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:2rem">{site.intro}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap about-grid" data-section="about-body">
    <div class="portrait">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt="Ryan Amarit"
        width={1280}
        widths={[480, 720, 960, 1280]}
        sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="prose-lg">
      <p>
        I started in the studio. I earned a B.F.A. in Visual Art from the University of North Texas,
        then a graduate certificate in computer science from Seattle University, and I have been
        building for the web for nine years.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today I am the Web Development Tech Lead at 8am (formerly AffiniPay). I lead the platform
        behind eight brand websites, the Tailwind and Storybook design system they share, and the
        Contentful tools content teams publish with. I set the web team's priorities with Marketing,
        Growth, Design, Brand and Content, and I lead one other developer.
      </p>
      <p>
        The through-line is the same as it was in the studio: composition, rhythm, where the eye lands
        first. I care about the moment a page becomes legible, the code underneath it, and whether it
        still works for someone on a phone with a screen reader and reduced motion on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Away from work I build side projects, including RulerIQ, a pre-launch SaaS that shows brands
        which pages AI assistants cite.
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        {site.facts.map((fact) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
            <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>

      <p style="margin-top:2.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/projects/">See the work</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
